(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-02","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["午后日头正毒，沈砚踩着枯白水草下到南坡渠底。执事堂曾[[accuse|指控]]药农偷水，他却从泥沙与黏土的[[proportion|比例]]看出，急流是骤然停下的。青石壁上有几道新撬出的[[fracture|裂缝]]，深处还响着水声。水并未消失，而是走进了[[underground|地下的]]石缝。罗清举灯跟来，提醒他先找退路。他将绳子系在井旁树上，再用银扣试开渠壁的小门；石板移开，冷风从黑暗里扑到脸上。","石门下是一间废弃的值守室。壁图上三道原本[[symmetrical|对称的]]分水槽，如今一边的刻线被石灰糊住。沈砚扒开灰屑，试着[[interpret|解读]]褪色标注：药田不是水路的终点，多余泉水本该继续下山。罗清捡起残破算板，[[calculate|计算]]近十日的取水量，发现山门所得已是旧额的三倍。有人磨平刻痕，想[[erase|抹去]]谷中的份额，却没来得及清掉壁角的旧水线。黑沙水和干田，原来出自同一次改渠。","桌边放着一本过于整齐的[[counterfeit|伪造的]]账册，火盆里却卡着半片焦黑的旧纸。沈砚托起这枚[[fragment|残片]]，把它的水印与母亲旧契作[[comparison|对比]]，看见同年的造纸纹。缺失的两行终于有了着落：药田守户不得让任何一家独占水门。土地的[[possession|所有权]]原来还带着护渠的义务。他一直以为母亲只是替自己留下一块田，却从未问过，她为何总将银扣泡在水里。","头顶忽然响起脚步，有人说周伯正在奉命养伤，随即一刀割断井外的绳子。沈砚将罗清推离落石，贴着墙检查开门的[[mechanism|机关]]。强撬一扇门会锁死另外两扇，他们只能找准槽口的[[alignment|对齐位置]]，让银扣带动旧轴。罗清在图角找到守渠人留的应急[[outlet|出口]]。两人刚爬进雨沟，重石便砸进井口，沉闷的[[echo|回声]]沿石壁追来。沈砚用肩护住账纸，左袖被碎石撕开一道口子。","罗清的灯碎了，沈砚的绳、水和通行文书也落在井里。纸只能证明改过账，要问是谁改的，还得找到活着的[[witness|证人]]。罗清说周伯曾参与立约，东渡口的旧庙是他躲雨的地方。沈砚照着账页箭头[[orient|辨明方向]]，把剩下的铜钱交给她，请她[[arrange|安排]]一条能过河的船。此时回山只会被当作偷账，他们必须先[[recover|找回]]失踪的守渠人。天边还有一点红，两人踩着雨沟，向河岸赶去。"],"en":["Under the harsh afternoon sun, Shen climbed into the dry channel through brittle white weeds. The clerks had chosen to [[accuse|accuse]] the growers of stealing water, but the [[proportion|proportion]] of sand to clay showed an abrupt stop in a fast current. Fresh [[fracture|fractures]] marked the stone wall, and water murmured behind them. It had not vanished; it had entered an [[underground|underground]] passage. Luo followed with a lamp and reminded him to secure a way out. He tied a rope to the tree beside the well, then tried the silver clasp in a small wall door. The stone moved, and cold air struck his face.","Below was an abandoned keeper's room. Its wall drawing showed three once [[symmetrical|symmetrical]] channels, with the marks on one side covered in lime. Shen scraped it away and tried to [[interpret|interpret]] the faded labels. The herb fields were not the route's end; surplus water should have continued downhill. Luo found a broken counting board and began to [[calculate|calculate]] consumption over the previous ten days. The mountain had taken three times its old allowance. Someone had tried to [[erase|erase]] the valley's share by grinding down the marks, but an old water line remained in a corner. The black sand and dry fields came from the same alteration.","An unusually tidy [[counterfeit|counterfeit]] ledger lay beside the desk, while a scorched piece of older paper remained in the brazier. Shen lifted the [[fragment|fragment]] and made a [[comparison|comparison]] between its watermark and his mother's deed. They bore the same year's pattern. The missing lines were now clear: the field's keeper must prevent any household from taking sole control of the water gate. Land [[possession|possession]] carried a duty to protect the channel. He had always thought his mother had left him only a field. He had never asked why she kept the silver clasp in water.","Footsteps sounded overhead. Someone said Zhou was resting under orders, then cut the rope outside the well. Shen pushed Luo away from the falling stones and examined the door [[mechanism|mechanism]]. Forcing one door would lock the other two. They had to find the correct [[alignment|alignment]] of the grooves so the clasp could turn the old shaft. Luo found the keeper's emergency [[outlet|outlet]] in a corner of the drawing. They had barely crawled into a rain ditch when a heavy stone struck the well. Its dull [[echo|echo]] followed along the walls. Shen shielded the papers with his shoulder, and a sharp fragment tore his left sleeve.","Luo's lamp was broken. Shen's rope, water and travel papers remained in the well. The documents showed alterations, but identifying their author required a living [[witness|witness]]. Luo said Zhou had helped establish the agreement and sometimes sheltered in the old temple at the eastern crossing. Shen used the ledger's arrow to [[orient|orient]] himself, then gave her his remaining coins to [[arrange|arrange]] a boat. Returning now would leave them accused of stealing records. First they had to [[recover|recover]] the missing keeper. With a little red still in the sky, they followed the rain ditch toward the river."]});
